#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) test exercising the FOURTH-ORDER
hyper-resistive term in the generalized Ohm's law, in addition to the full set of
terms (convection + Hall + resistive eta*J + electron pressure gradient).

This is the companion regression case to ../hybrid_ohm/PARAM.in. The same
geometry and ion-scale normalization are used (d_i ~ v_A ~ 1 in code units). The
hyper-resistivity (eta_h * nabla^2 J) is added to demonstrate damping of the
grid-scale / PIC shot-noise that the second-order eta*J term cannot reach.

Use HYPERRESISTIVITY etaHyperMode = "grid" (the default) so eta_h is scaled to
the CFL-stable bound on each sub-step:
    eta_h = 4*pi * C_h * dx_min^4 / dt_sub
with C_h = etaHyperCh (here 1e-3, a mild damping). "si" mode (direct SI [m^4/s])
is also supported and is what a dispersion validation would use.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#RESISTIVITY
1000000.0               etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
5.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

#HYPERRESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaHyperSI      [m^4/s; unused in grid mode]
grid                    etaHyperMode
0.001                   etaHyperCh

Minimum charge-density floor for the 1/rho factors (auto = 1e-6*density here).
#DENSITYFLOOR
0.0                     rhoFloorHybrid

Use the compact staggered current (default T). Set F to fall back to the legacy
2*dx collocated curl (regression against pre-change baselines).
#HYBRIDCURL
T                       useCompactCurl

#HALLSUBCYCLE
32                      nHallSubcycle

#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
5.2195e-9               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
5.0e4                   uNormSI   [m/s] ~ v_A so v_A ~ 1 in code units

#MONITOR
1                       dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
0.5                     dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez       varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
6.25                    TimeMax

#RUN
